From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 09:15:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06871/11362] [outer-loop] ARC ka59 round-5: tooling failure,
 prefix confirmed but no exploration

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on ka59 confirmed the 358-action prefix
replays cleanly to level 6, but its own frame-only diagnostic printer
crashed on ka59's two-layer 64x64 rendered frame tensor (it assumed a
single-layer grid), terminating the live environment before any
post-prefix exploration. Agent-tooling bug, not a game finding -- future
attempts must handle the multi-layer frame shape explicitly.

No registry count change, frontier stays at level 6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
